course: everyday
lesson: 27
title: Caring for pets
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pet depends on you for everything it needs: the right food, fresh clean water every day, a clean place to live, exercise, company and gentle handling.
explain: Every kind of animal needs its own kind of care: a dog needs walks, a rabbit needs hay, space and a rabbit friend, a hamster sleeps in the day and is awake at night, and a fish needs a clean tank, not a tiny bowl.
explain: Some human foods are poisonous to pets: chocolate, grapes, raisins, onions and sweets with xylitol can make a dog very ill, and lilies are deadly to cats.
explain: Pets need a vet for check-ups, vaccinations and whenever they seem ill, hurt, stop eating or act strangely.
explain: Kindness means handling animals gently, never teasing them, letting them rest, and remembering that a pet is a promise for its whole life, not a toy for a few weeks.
explain: A family in Texas left their dog in the car for ten minutes on a warm day; the car heated up like an oven, and the dog collapsed from the heat.
explain: A boy in Leeds gave his dog chocolate as a treat; the dog was sick, shaking and had to go to the vet.
fact: Pets need fresh, clean water every day.
fact: Each kind of pet needs its own kind of food.
fact: Chocolate, grapes, raisins and onions can poison dogs.
fact: Lilies are very poisonous to cats, even the pollen.
fact: A vet is an animal doctor who gives check-ups, treatment and vaccinations (injections that protect a pet from serious diseases).
fact: Rabbits need lots of hay, room to hop and usually another rabbit for company.
fact: Hamsters are awake at night and should not be woken up in the day.
fact: Rabbits must never be picked up by their ears.
fact: Dogs need daily walks and exercise.
fact: A pet that stops eating or acts strangely may be ill and should see a vet.
fact: Teasing an animal is unkind and can teach it to bite or scratch.
fact: Some pets live a long time: cats and dogs often live 10 to 15 years or more.
fact: Chocolate, grapes and raisins can poison dogs.
fact: A parked car can get dangerously hot within minutes, even when it is not very hot outside.
exercise: What must every pet have every single day? | Fresh, clean water | A new toy | A bath | A ride in the car to the park
exercise: Which of these is poisonous to dogs? | Chocolate | Plain cooked chicken | Carrots | Dog biscuits
exercise: Which flower is very dangerous to cats? | The lily | The sunflower | The daisy | The rose
exercise: What is a vet? | A doctor for animals | A person who sells pets | A shop for pet food | A pet trainer for dogs
exercise: What does a rabbit need most of in its food? | Hay | Chocolate | Bread | Cheese
exercise: When is a hamster usually awake? | At night | Only at midday | All day and never at night | Only in winter
exercise: How should you never pick up a rabbit? | By its ears | With both hands supporting its body | Gently close to your chest | With an adult's help
exercise: Your dog suddenly stops eating and lies still all day. What should you do? | Tell an adult so the dog can see a vet | Give it chocolate to cheer it up and get it eating | Leave it until next month | Take it for a very long run
exercise: Why do dogs need walks every day? | They need exercise and things to sniff and explore | Walks make their fur grow | Dogs cannot sleep at night unless they have walked for hours | Walks stop them from needing water
exercise: Why is it unkind to tease a pet? | It frightens the pet and can teach it to bite | Pets enjoy being teased, it is like a game to them | Teasing makes pets smarter | Pets do not notice teasing
exercise: Why do vets give pets vaccinations? | To protect them from serious diseases | To make them grow faster and bigger than other pets | To change their fur colour | To make them sleep better
exercise: Which is a good home for a goldfish? | A large, clean tank with a filter | A small bowl that is never cleaned | A glass of tap water | A bucket kept in the dark
exercise: Why might a rabbit kept on its own be unhappy? | Rabbits are social and like company of other rabbits | Rabbits hate all other animals | Rabbits need to live with cats | Rabbits only like to be alone, so it must be ill instead
exercise: How long can a pet dog or cat live? | Often 10 to 15 years or more | About one year | Only a few months | Always more than 50 years
test: Zoe in Vancouver wants to share her chocolate bar with her dog as a treat. Why should she not? | Chocolate can poison dogs | Dogs do not like sweet things | It will make the dog's teeth fall out at once | Chocolate makes dogs bark all night
test: Harry's family in Wales brings home a bunch of lilies. They have a cat. What should they do? | Keep the lilies out of the house | Put them on the cat's food bowl | Let the cat sniff them to learn | Nothing, lilies are safe for cats
test: Which is true? | A hamster sleeps in the day and wakes at night | A hamster sleeps all night like us | A rabbit is happiest on its own in a tiny hutch | Fish do not need clean water
test: Mia's rabbit has had no fresh water since yesterday. Why is this a problem? | Animals need clean water every day to stay healthy | Rabbits get all the water they need from the morning air | Water is only needed in summer | Rabbits drink once a week
test: A boy wakes his hamster at noon to play. Why might it bite him? | It was woken from its daytime sleep and is scared | Hamsters bite whenever they are hungry, whatever the time | It thinks his finger is a carrot | Hamsters always bite at noon
test: A family wants a puppy for Christmas, and the children promise to look after it «for a while». What have they forgotten? | A dog needs care for its whole life, often over ten years | Puppies only live for one year | Dogs look after themselves | Puppies stay small forever
test: What is the kindest way to handle a pet? | Gently, letting it rest when it wants | Squeezing it tightly so it cannot escape | Chasing it to give it exercise | Holding it up high by its legs
test: Why do pets need check-ups at the vet even when they seem well? | A vet can catch problems early and give vaccinations | Vets give pets new names | Pets get bored at home | Check-ups make pets grow taller and stronger than other pets
test: A girl in Adelaide keeps her goldfish in a small bowl that she never cleans. What will happen? | The water gets dirty and the fish gets ill | The fish cleans the water itself | The fish grows into a big fish | Nothing, fish do not need clean water
test: can the dog have a bit of my chocolate | No, chocolate can poison dogs | Yes, just a small piece is fine | Yes, dark chocolate only | Yes, if it's a treat day
test: nan brought lilies, cat's sniffing em | Keep them away, lilies poison cats | It's fine, cats love flowers | Only the leaves are bad | Only the stems are bad
test: hamster's asleep, wake him to play? | No, hamsters sleep in the day | Yes, he wants to play now with you | Yes, tap the cage | Yes, if you're gentle
test: dog hasn't eaten all day and is acting weird | Take him to the vet | He's just fussy | Give him chocolate | Wait a few weeks
test: can i give the dog some of my chocolate, he's begging | No, chocolate can poison dogs | Yes, a small bit is fine | Yes, if it is milk chocolate | Yes, if he eats it slowly
test: we're popping into the shop, leave the dog in the car? | No, cars get hot fast and the dog can die | Yes, if it is only ten minutes | Yes, if you crack a window open for air | Yes, if the car is in the sun
test: forgot to give the hamster water for 3 days | Give it water now and tell an adult, it may be ill | It is fine, hamsters do not drink | Give it extra food instead | Wait and see if it gets thirsty
test: did u hear the Taylors' dog nearly died cos it ate a whole box of chocolates at Easter | Real lesson: chocolate can poison dogs, so keep it out of reach | Real lesson: dogs only get sick from Easter eggs, not other chocolate | It proves dogs should not be kept at Easter | It is gossip, so chocolate is fine for dogs
test: my cousin says u should pick a rabbit up by the ears, that's how farmers do it | That is wrong and cruel; rabbits must never be picked up by their ears | He is right, ears are the strongest part | He is right, if the rabbit is small | He is right, farmers know best about rabbits
test: someone says Zara's hamster died cos she forgot to feed it, everyone's talking about it | Do not spread it; she is probably sad and the rumour may be untrue | Spread it, because it is a lesson for everyone | Spread it, so she never gets another pet | Spread it, and add that she did not care
exam: Which of the following foods are recognised as poisonous to dogs? | Chocolate, grapes, raisins and onions | Carrots, rice, plain chicken and water | Apples without seeds and green beans | Cooked eggs and plain pumpkin
exam: Identify the hazard presented by lilies to domestic cats. | Lilies, including their pollen, are severely poisonous to cats | Lilies are harmful to cats only when eaten in large quantity | Lilies are harmless to cats but poisonous to dogs | Lilies cause cats merely to sneeze
exam: Select the response that is consistent with the established facts concerning the requirements of rabbits. | Rabbits require abundant hay, room in which to hop and, usually, another rabbit as company | Rabbits require only pellets and a small cage | Rabbits prefer to live alone without company | Rabbits require no fresh water if given vegetables
exam: It is given that a pet has ceased eating and conducts itself strangely. Determine the appropriate course of action. | The pet should be examined by a veterinary surgeon | The pet should be given chocolate to restore its appetite | The pet should be left alone for some weeks | The pet should be exercised more vigorously
